<title>UK: UK May net consumer credit up 1.105 bln stg in May.</title>
<headline>UK May net consumer credit up 1.105 bln stg in May.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK consumer credit grew by a net s/a 1.105 billion stg in May, after a revised 806 million stg increase in April, Bank of England data showed.  </p>
<p>Following are May consumer credit data for May - (previously released data in brackets, in MLN STG)</p>
<p>				 May	  April	  May 96</p>
<p>TOTAL NET LENDING	   3,127    2,535(2,494)  2,364</p>
<p>  -- Consumer credit	1,105	 806(691)     703</p>
<p>  -- Secured on dwellings 2,022    1,725(1,803)   1,660</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN of net consumer lending BY SOURCE -</p>
<p>  -- Banks		     903     679(578)	  517</p>
<p>  -- Building societies     18	19(19)	    33</p>
<p>  -- Other spec lenders    139	95 (n/a)	 172</p>
<p>  -- Retailers		  30	-2(3)	     -9</p>
<p>  -- Insurers		   15	14(n/a)	  -10</p>
<p>CREDIT CARD		    307     136 (126)	 159</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted, in PCT)</p>
<p> Total personal borrowing mth/mth  0.6    0.5(0.5) 0.5</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;    3mth/3mth 7.0    7.0(n/a) 6.4</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;     yr/yr    7.0    6.8(6.9) 5.5</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     1.4    1.1(0.9) 1.0</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;     3mth/3mth	  15.3  16.2(n/a) 17.6</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;     yr/yr		17.0  16.6(16.5)14.6</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
